  "goodToKnow": "Horchen means to listen intently, often secretly: an der Wand horchen. It's a bit old-fashioned; hören (to hear) and zuhören (to listen) are everyday words. Aufhorchen means to prick up one's ears, and lauschen (to listen attentively) is more poetic. Note that its participle gehorcht is identical to that of gehorchen (to obey). Der Horchposten was a listening post."
